; Axiom 6 from the sheet centre: the circle around .o through .a meets --bc at
; both .b and .c, so the two creases are the vertical midline and the
; anti-diagonal. Both cut the paper's interior, so the paper-incidence filter
; settles nothing and the ambiguity stands.

paper square
mark (through .a .c) as --ac
.o = free on --ac from .a at 1/2        ; the sheet centre, (1/2, 1/2)
--x = (map .a onto --bc through .o)

; expect error "two folds place .a onto --bc through .o, both landing on the paper"
